                <head>450. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Antarctic Treaty was negotiated at the Conference on Antarctica held in
                    Washington October 15–December 1, 1959; it was signed by 18 nations on December
                    1, 1959. For documentation on the sessions of the Conference, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg_580"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1958–1960, volume II, pages 580</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg_632">632</ref>. For text of the Treaty, see
                    12 UST 794 or <hi rendition="#italic">American Foreign Policy: Current
                        Documents, 1961</hi>, pages 452–458. The United States ratified the treaty
                    on August 18, 1960, and it came into effect on June 23, 1961, after ratification
                    by all the signatories.</p>
            </div>
